<title>USA: Express Scripts Q4 net up on member growth.</title>
<headline>Express Scripts Q4 net up on member growth.</headline>
<dateline>ST. LOUIS 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Express Scripts Inc said Thursday a surge in membership, along with improved cost controls, helped earnings and revenue increase in the fourth quarter ended December 31.</p>
<p>The healthcare management services company reported net income of $7.2 million, or $0.43 a share, compared to $4.7 million, or $0.31 a share one year ago. Revenues in the quarter climbed to $226.2 million from $152.8 million in 1995, Express Scripts said.</p>
<p>The company said it had 9.9 million members at the end of 1996, compared to 8.1 million in 1995.</p>
<p>Express Script shares were trading down 1/4 at 32-3/4.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
